{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00013",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 2.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Hello, please sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.4,
      "end_seconds": 4.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.52,
      "end_seconds": 6.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Busy day out there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.28,
      "end_seconds": 11.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Always is. The traffic coming in was terrible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.25,
      "end_seconds": 14.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "In your own words, what's happened?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.77,
      "end_seconds": 19.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "It's tingling in my fingers. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.07,
      "end_seconds": 24.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.45,
      "end_seconds": 38.75,
      "duration_seconds": 13.3,
      "text": "It happens once or twice a day. I get some relief from shaking my hand. I'd say mild. My family kept telling me to get it checked. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.34,
      "end_seconds": 42.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.96,
      "end_seconds": 48.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "It usually comes with numbness in the thumb and first two fingers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.2,
      "end_seconds": 52.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Have you been waking up at night with pins and needles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.26,
      "end_seconds": 61.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, one week. The, The numbness in the thumb and first two fingers? That's been since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.77,
      "end_seconds": 67.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Have you had tingling in your fingers before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.64,
      "end_seconds": 73.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.21,
      "end_seconds": 88.73,
      "duration_seconds": 14.52,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.27,
      "end_seconds": 91.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.93,
      "end_seconds": 98.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any neck pain, trouble walking or swelling in the joints?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.7,
      "end_seconds": 100.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.27,
      "end_seconds": 104.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Any headache, weakness in the legs or bladder problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.98,
      "end_seconds": 110.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "No, no headache, weakness in the legs or bladder problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.12,
      "end_seconds": 113.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.71,
      "end_seconds": 116.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 119.25,
      "end_seconds": 126.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. BP is 117 over 73, respiratory rate 18, temperature is 36.6 degrees, pulse 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.74,
      "end_seconds": 132.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.2,
      "end_seconds": 138.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.56,
      "end_seconds": 141.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.35,
      "end_seconds": 146.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "I had cataract surgery on my right eye last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.52,
      "end_seconds": 149.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.36,
      "end_seconds": 152.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.56,
      "end_seconds": 173.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Moving on to your background, any past medical history? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.77,
      "end_seconds": 182.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Yes, an underactive thyroid. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I've got diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.88,
      "end_seconds": 191.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.71,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known an underactive thyroid. We'll keep that in mind today. So, yes, I can see the diabetes in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.11,
      "end_seconds": 195.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Hold on, the screen's frozen for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.29,
      "end_seconds": 212.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Alright, back to you. What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.62,
      "end_seconds": 219.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "Thyroxine. I take it 75 micrograms, every morning. Metformin. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 219.96,
      "end_seconds": 223.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 250 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.49,
      "end_seconds": 229.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.58,
      "end_seconds": 233.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.63,
      "end_seconds": 245.85,
      "duration_seconds": 11.22,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.72,
      "end_seconds": 250.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.14,
      "end_seconds": 258.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Okay, do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.52,
      "end_seconds": 261.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "So, no, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.97,
      "end_seconds": 265.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.8,
      "end_seconds": 267.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.66,
      "end_seconds": 270.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.39,
      "end_seconds": 291.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Bending the wrist for a minute brings on the numbness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.81,
      "end_seconds": 294.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.9,
      "end_seconds": 304.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Power in the thumb is slightly reduced."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.15,
      "end_seconds": 318.59,
      "duration_seconds": 11.44,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.04,
      "end_seconds": 331.86,
      "duration_seconds": 11.82,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.3,
      "end_seconds": 340.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like carpal tunnel syndrome. I'd also keep diabetic neuropathy in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.33,
      "end_seconds": 343.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.84,
      "end_seconds": 361.44,
      "duration_seconds": 16.6,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now carpal tunnel syndrome is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had tingling in your fingers, mild, and no bladder problems or weakness in the legs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.56,
      "end_seconds": 365.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Yes, uh, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.62,
      "end_seconds": 381.17,
      "duration_seconds": 14.55,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.55,
      "end_seconds": 386.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.16,
      "end_seconds": 390.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "We should do a nerve conduction study for hand numbness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.25,
      "end_seconds": 393.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.59,
      "end_seconds": 398.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "I'm going to order a blood sugar test, for neuropathy screen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.85,
      "end_seconds": 401.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.52,
      "end_seconds": 417.54,
      "duration_seconds": 16.02,
      "text": "A night wrist splint, kept neutral, usually helps a lot. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 418.85,
      "end_seconds": 421.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Okay, uh, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.1,
      "end_seconds": 428.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.59,
      "end_seconds": 429.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 430.43,
      "end_seconds": 437.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Let's review you in four weeks. Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 438.18,
      "end_seconds": 441.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "So, I come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 443.15,
      "end_seconds": 446.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.13,
      "end_seconds": 448.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "No questions. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.67,
      "end_seconds": 450.37,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}